[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
open-media-drc — post-install checklist
=======================================

1. Configuration
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/omdrc.conf.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/omdrc.conf
   and edit (GEOMETRY, state dir).  The stack ships with FLAT (identity)
   filters — audio passes through unchanged until you install real room
   correction filters; see FILTERS_AND_DRC.md in the docs.

2. BruteFIR defaults (REQUIRED — brutefir fails to start without it):
   as the audio user:
     mkdir -p ~/.config/BruteFIR
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/brutefir_defaults.conf.sample \
        ~/.config/BruteFIR/brutefir_defaults.conf
   Adjust the OSS device paths inside if your DAC is not /dev/dsp0.

3. Kernel modules (in /etc/rc.conf or kld_list):
     kld_list="cuse"          # required by virtual_oss

4. MPD outputs: merge the example MPD config
   (%%PREFIX%%/share/examples/open-media-drc/musicpd.conf.in) into your mpd
   config — the OKTO-DAC / DRC-native / DRC-resamp output names are what
   drc.sh toggles with mpc.

5. Services, in /etc/rc.conf:
     musicpd_enable="YES"
     drc_usb_audio_enable="YES"
     brutefir_drc_user="<audio user>"
   Do NOT set brutefir_drc_enable — brutefir_drc is the worker that
   drc_usb_audio drives (boot probe + devd hotplug).

6. devd hotplug (start/stop DRC on DAC plug/unplug):
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/devd/usb-audio-drc.conf.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/devd/usb-audio-drc.conf
     service devd restart

7. Run `omdrc 192000` (or omdrc resamp / off / status) to drive the chain
   manually; state persists in /var/db/omdrc (root) — pin OMDRC_STATE_DIR in
   omdrc.conf so services and interactive runs share it.
EOM
}
]
